Reject patterns with more approximate bounds than the approximate
matcher keeps costs for.

tre_expand_ast() gives each approximate bound in a pattern its own
parameter depth (the copies of a repeated bound share one), and
tre_tnfa_run_approx() keeps costs for depths 0 to TRE_M_MAX_DEPTH (3)
only, checked by an assert() in tre_set_params().  R maps that assert()
to an R error, so a pattern such as "a{~1}b{~1}c{~1}d{~1}" fails with
"assertion 'value <= 3' failed in executing regexp", which the harnesses
discard; with instrumentation/0009 it aborts instead, and the agrep
target would stop at the first stored input with four such bounds.
Stock TRE builds, which compile the assert() out, write past the cost
table.  Make tre_compile() reject such patterns with REG_ESPACE, as for
TRE's other size limits.

Upstream status: laurikari/tre PR #172 (r-devel/tre branch
bugfix/approx-param-depth, in its r-integration branch); r-devel/r-svn
PR #537 re-vendors that branch (no Bugzilla report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

diff --git a/src/extra/tre/tre-compile.c b/src/extra/tre/tre-compile.c
index 39eff64a0f..df614dde06 100644
--- a/src/extra/tre/tre-compile.c
+++ b/src/extra/tre/tre-compile.c
@@ -2187,6 +2187,8 @@ tre_compile(regex_t *preg, const tre_char_t *regex, size_t n, int cflags)
 			   &tnfa->params_depth);
   if (errcode != REG_OK)
     ERROR_EXIT(errcode);
+  if (tnfa->params_depth > TRE_M_MAX_DEPTH)
+    ERROR_EXIT(REG_ESPACE);
 
   /* Add a dummy node for the final state.
      XXX - For certain patterns this dummy node can be optimized away,
diff --git a/src/extra/tre/tre-internal.h b/src/extra/tre/tre-internal.h
index 7db0ebb489..a19534e623 100644
--- a/src/extra/tre/tre-internal.h
+++ b/src/extra/tre/tre-internal.h
@@ -302,6 +302,11 @@ typedef enum {
   TRE_PARAM_LAST	    = 9
 } tre_param_t;
 
+/* Largest TRE_PARAM_DEPTH the approximate matcher has room for.  Each
+   approximate bound in a pattern gets its own depth, so this is also
+   the most approximate bounds a pattern can have. */
+#define TRE_M_MAX_DEPTH 3
+
 /* Unset matching parameter */
 #define TRE_PARAM_UNSET -1
 
